  "summary": "Seven preprints show fMRI and EEG measures of dynamics, entropy, and coupling tracking altered states, expertise, and cognition in November 2026.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is that brain activity is characterized as state-dependent dynamics on a constrained structural or low-dimensional scaffold rather than as fixed regional function. Breathwork and jhana EEG studies report desynchronization, flattened hierarchy, and increased entropy complexity, with jhana complexity dissociated from experiential measures. Dance expertise is linked to higher local brain entropy and shared responses. Structure-function coupling varies with cognitive state, strongest during movie-watching and weakest under working memory load. Oddball detection follows shared low-dimensional brain-state dimensions with modality-dependent later trajectories. Meta-analytic work frames the self as shifting coalitions of distributed systems, and HCP resting-state data link spatial and temporal organization to trait-like dynamics. Evidence is preprint-only and spans heterogeneous methods and samples.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
